    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d885">

                <pb facs="0706" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12982.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-24T16:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the interview this morning we were informed that General Carranza has not
                    assumed the title of President. The proper address is First Chief in charge of
                    the Executive Authority.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
